itical width as a function of training fraction; a sweep of the hidden-layer exponent (a script exists but was not run); a sweep of the output-scaling exponent and unembedding scale; an intervention on weight decay; and any weight-norm or circuit-level diagnostics. Nothing in the main text depends on them.\n9:      \"figure_type\": \"diagram\",\n38:      \"figure_type\": \"interval_plot\",\n72:      \"figure_type\": \"dot_plot\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
